gaoM(){return"View full guide"},
ga_c(){return"What do you grow?"},
gasg(){return"Start with what you grow most. Add the rest later."},
gasd(){return"No crops yet"},
gas8(){return"Add the first one"},
gas9(){return"Add another"},
gase(){return"Enter the app"},
gasf(){return"Icon"},
gasc(){return"Done"},
gasa(){return"Fill in details\u2026"},
gape(){return"Crop added"},
gapc(){return"Add another"},
gapd(){return"Crop added. Do you want to register another crop already planted on your farm?"},
gapf(){return"Enter, I'm done"},
ga1j(){return"+ Create new crop\u2026"},
galE(){return"Learn to run Balance"},
galQ(){return"Start"},
galP(){return"Routine"},
galR(){return"Understand"},
galD(){return"Choose how your farm is today. In five minutes you'll make your first entry."},
galC(){return"How is your farm today?"},
galB(){return"Examples use round numbers and \u201cyour currency.\u201d They work the same for any country and any crop."},
gaks(){return"I already sell what I harvest"},
gakr(){return"You have crops producing fruit and want to know if you're making money."},
gaku(){return"I'm about to start"},
gakt(){return"You're going to plant and want to see how much you invest before harvesting."},
gakq(){return"I'm going to renew or expand"},
gakp(){return"You're going to replace plants or add area to a crop."},
gakw(){return"I have workers"},
gakv(){return"You pay daily wages and want the cost to land on the right crop."},
galn(){return"Don't record what already happened. Start today: what you spend and what you sell."},
galp(){return"Check your crops: Crops \u203a your crop. Set the phase to \u201cProducing\u201d and, if you know them, the area and plants. If you don't, leave them empty: the app doesn't invent."},
galq(){return"Record your first expense: Record \u203a Expense. Choose the crop and category: fertilizer, labor, transport. If the expense is for several crops, split it by area or percentage."},
galr(){return"Record your first sale: Record \u203a Income. Enter the kilos and what you were paid. With those kilos, that crop's harvest is recorded automatically. Don't record it twice."},
gals(){return"Check the month: Overview or Report. There you see income, expenses, balance and cost per kilo. The report exports to PDF or Excel."},
galm(){return"Example with coffee, 2 ha and 3,000 plants"},
gali(){return"Expense: 500 in fertilizer, assigned to coffee."},
galj(){return"Sale: 50 kg for 750."},
galk(){return"Result: income 750 \xb7 expenses 500 \xb7 balance 250 \xb7 cost per kilo 10."},
galh(){return"What you sold before using the app isn't needed: the report starts with what you record."},
galo(){return"If you have several crops on the same land, assign them when you record the expense; the app splits it by area or percentage."},
galK(){return"While the crop isn't producing, the app doesn't tell you that you're losing money: it shows how much you've invested. It's an investment, not a bad month."},
galL(){return"Create the crop: Crops \u203a New crop. Name, phase \u201cNot producing yet\u201d and whether it's perennial or annual. Area and plants can stay empty."},
galM(){return"Record the planting: Plantings \u203a New planting. How many plants, in what area and the date. If you enter the cost, the app creates the linked expense for you: don't repeat it in Record."},
galN(){return"Record what you invest: Record \u203a Expense, with the crop. Fertilizer, labor, tools. Everything before the first harvest shows as investment."},
galO(){return"When you harvest, change the phase: Crops \u203a your crop \u203a phase \u201cProducing.\u201d From then on, the sale records the harvest."},
galJ(){return"Example with corn, 1 ha and 20,000 plants"},
galF(){return"Planting: 20,000 plants on 1 ha."},
galG(){return"Investment: 300 in seed + 200 in preparation = 500."},
galH(){return"Before harvesting: 500 invested, no loss."},
galI(){return"First sale: 1,000 kg for 800. The harvest is recorded."},
gakR(){return"Don't delete the old crop. The app keeps its history and adds the new part."},
gakS(){return"Choose what happens to the old plants: Plantings \u203a New planting. If you replace part of them, choose \u201cRenew a part\u201d and the lot you're renewing. Old plants go down and new ones add up: the total doesn't inflate."},
gakT(){return"If you're expanding, don't replace: choose \u201cExpand the crop.\u201d You add area and plants without touching what was already there."},
gakU(){return"Check the new age: the renewed lot starts its own age. Old harvests stay in the history and in the report."},
gakQ(){return"Example with 3,000 coffee plants; you renew 1,000"},
gakN(){return"Planting: 1,000 new plants, \u201cRenew a part,\u201d old lot."},
gakO(){return"Total: still 3,000, not 4,000."},
gakP(){return"The new lot has its date; the old one keeps its own."},
gamc(){return"A wage isn't a loose expense: it goes to the crop where they worked. That's how cost per kilo tells the truth."},
gamh(){return"Save the worker: Workers \u203a New worker. Name and daily pay. If the wage changes, update it there."},
gami(){return"Record the payment: Record \u203a Expense \u203a Labor. Choose the worker, the days and the crop. The app calculates the amount; if you paid something else, adjust it."},
gamj(){return"If it was harvest work, mark it: in the task choose \u201cHarvest,\u201d enter the kilos and the lot. That gives you the pickup cost per kilo."},
gamk(){return"Check payroll: Report \u203a Payroll of the period. There you see how many days and how much you paid each person."},
